{"resourceIdentifier":"1116","resourceName":"St Joseph Sanitary Landfill Gas Collection and Control System","description":"The St. Joseph Sanitary Landfill (Landfill) began operation in 1978 and is located on a 156-acre site located in St. Joseph, Missouri.  The Landfill’s current disposal area is approximately 88 acres with three (3) cells (Areas 1, 2, and 3).    In 2011, the existing landfill gas collection system was expanded from 17 wells to 47 wells in order to collect enough high quality gas to support a landfill gas to energy plant that was also installed.  In addition, the open flare was replaced with an enclosed flare and a new gas conditioning skid and metering system were installed.  The landfill gas to energy facility began operating in December 2011 and is the primary destruction device for the landfill gas, with the flare serving as back-up.","location":{"latitude":39.675329,"longitude":-94.775286},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1116"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"MO"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Kansas City Power and Light Greater Missouri"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"41000"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0001"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Ruby Canyon Engineering, Inc"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"25/10/2013"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CREDITING PERIOD HAS EXPIRED, 02/12/2011 - 01/12/2021"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCU